WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
Once upon a time, a donkey lived on a farm.

2
00:00:05.021 --> 00:00:08.776
The donkey worked hard for the farmer.

3
00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:14.539
After many years the donkey became old and tired.

4
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:21.479
"Oh, this sack is so heavy! I wish I could rest."

5
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:27.316
"Hmm, this donkey is getting too old to work for me any longer.

6
00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:32.294
I should sell him to the butcher."

7
00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:37.823
"Oh no! The butcher will kill me. I must escape.

8
00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:42.598
Hmm, but what will I do for a living then?

9
00:00:42.599 --> 00:00:51.702
Ah! I will go to Bremen and become a musician."

10
00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:55.918
The farmer and the donkey returned to the farm.

11
00:00:55.919 --> 00:01:01.840
The farmer took the donkey's sack and went into the barn.

12
00:01:01.841 --> 00:01:04.612
"Now is my chance!"

13
00:01:04.613 --> 00:01:11.541
The donkey ran away.

14
00:01:11.542 --> 00:01:15.038
Soon the donkey found the road to Bremen.

15
00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:21.446
He met an old dog lying on the road. The dog was out of breath.

16
00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:27.184
"Why are you out of breath, Mr. Dog?"

17
00:01:27.185 --> 00:01:32.449
"Ah! I am old and weak. I cannot hunt anymore.

18
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:38.828
My master thought I was lazy, so he tried to shoot me. I ran away.

19
00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:47.600
But now I do not have either a home or a job. I will starve."

20
00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:53.294
"I am going to Bremen to become a musician. Let's go together.

21
00:01:53.295 --> 00:02:03.275
We can start a musical band. I will play the guitar, and you can beat the drum."

22
00:02:03.276 --> 00:02:06.840
"That's a great idea!"

23
00:02:06.841 --> 00:02:13.761
The donkey and the dog walked towards Bremen.

24
00:02:13.762 --> 00:02:23.057
Before long they met a cat. He was sitting beside the road. The cat had a sad look.

25
00:02:23.058 --> 00:02:30.565
"Mr. Cat, you look so sad. What's the matter with you?"

26
00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:36.690
"I am sad because I am no longer loved. I am too old to catch mice anymore.

27
00:02:36.691 --> 00:02:43.290
And my mistress beat me. So I ran away. But I don't know where to go."

28
00:02:43.291 --> 00:02:49.510
"Oh, come with us to Bremen. We can start a musical band.

29
00:02:49.511 --> 00:02:59.435
I will play the guitar, Mr. Dog can beat the drum, and you can sing in our band."

30
00:02:59.436 --> 00:03:02.489
"That sounds great!"

31
00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:08.912
So the cat joined the dog and the donkey on their way to Bremen.

32
00:03:08.913 --> 00:03:15.336
Soon the three animals came to a farm. A rooster sat on the fence.

33
00:03:15.337 --> 00:03:20.657
He crowed with all his might. "Cock-a-doodle-doo!"

34
00:03:20.658 --> 00:03:26.025
"You sound scared. What is the matter?"

35
00:03:26.026 --> 00:03:29.874
"I wake up everyone on the farm every morning.

36
00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.265
But tonight guests are coming for dinner.

37
00:03:32.266 --> 00:03:36.075
The master's wife told the cook to cook me for their soup.

38
00:03:36.076 --> 00:03:42.536
So I am crowing until I die. Cock-a-doodle-doo!"

39
00:03:42.537 --> 00:03:49.043
"Mr. Rooster, you must come with us too. We are going to Bremen.

40
00:03:49.044 --> 00:03:56.823
You have a good voice. You can sing in our band."

41
00:03:56.824 --> 00:04:01.206
"Anything is better than death! I will join you right now."

42
00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:04.822
The rooster jumped down from the fence.

43
00:04:04.823 --> 00:04:10.216
Then all of the animals walked toward Bremen.

44
00:04:10.217 --> 00:04:14.140
That evening the animals passed through a forest.

45
00:04:14.141 --> 00:04:18.773
They decided to spend the night by a big tree.

46
00:04:18.774 --> 00:04:23.278
The donkey and the dog lay down near the tree.

47
00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:29.330
The cat climbed up the tree and curled up on a large branch.

48
00:04:29.331 --> 00:04:36.726
But the rooster flew up to the top of the tree. He could see all around them.

49
00:04:36.727 --> 00:04:43.461
"I see a light over there. It is a house. It is not too far from here!"

50
00:04:43.462 --> 00:04:46.203
"Let's spend the night in the house.

51
00:04:46.204 --> 00:04:50.116
It is too cold and windy to stay outside."

52
00:04:50.117 --> 00:04:57.211
"Yes, and there may be some food there too."

53
00:04:57.212 --> 00:05:04.292
The animals walked through the forest. Finally they reached the house.

54
00:05:04.293 --> 00:05:09.871
The donkey was the tallest, so he looked through the window.

55
00:05:09.872 --> 00:05:12.481
"What do you see, Mr. Donkey?"

56
00:05:12.482 --> 00:05:18.573
"Shush! Keep your voice down. Someone is in there."

57
00:05:18.574 --> 00:05:28.915
"Ohhh! We stole so much money. What a lucky day! Ha-ha-ha! Let's drink all night."

58
00:05:28.916 --> 00:05:33.361
"What do you see, Mr. Donkey?"

59
00:05:33.362 --> 00:05:37.063
"There are good things to eat and drink on the table.

60
00:05:37.064 --> 00:05:42.181
But robbers are sitting at the table too."

61
00:05:42.182 --> 00:05:48.769
"Robbers? Oh my. They might kill us. Let's run away!"

62
00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.909
"But I'm so hungry."

63
00:05:51.910 --> 00:06:01.535
"We can scare them away. Then we can eat the food and spend the night in the warm house."

64
00:06:01.536 --> 00:06:03.059
"How?"

65
00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:09.030
"I know how to scare them. I will put my front legs on the window ledge.

66
00:06:09.031 --> 00:06:17.572
Mr. Dog can jump on my back. Mr. Cat can climb on Mr. Dog's back.

67
00:06:17.573 --> 00:06:21.384
Mr. Rooster can fly to the very top.

68
00:06:21.385 --> 00:06:29.577
When I say 'Go,' we will all make noises as loudly as we can."

69
00:06:29.578 --> 00:06:33.717
The other animals thought that this was a great idea.

70
00:06:33.718 --> 00:06:42.565
They each climbed up on the donkey's back and waited for his signal. "Go!"

71
00:06:42.566 --> 00:06:52.385
"Cock-a-doodle-doo!" "Hee-haw, hee-haw!" "Meow, meeeooow!" "Bow-wow, ruff, ruff!"

72
00:06:52.386 --> 00:07:04.165
"Oh! It's a ghost! It is here to punish our sins. What should we do?"

73
00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:07.468
But the donkey was old and weak.

74
00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:11.446
He leaned against the window because he was tired.

75
00:07:11.447 --> 00:07:20.280
Suddenly the window broke. They all fell through the window and into the room.

76
00:07:20.281 --> 00:07:27.028
But fortunately the wind blew the candle out at the same time.

77
00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:38.742
"Ohhh! It's a ghost! Run!" The robbers ran out of the house thinking that a ghost made the noise and broke the window.

78
00:07:38.743 --> 00:07:46.896
Then the four animals laughed and sat down at the table. They ate and ate.

79
00:07:46.897 --> 00:07:57.431
Each animal found a comfortable spot and soon fell asleep.

80
00:07:57.432 --> 00:08:00.975
The robbers watched the house from the forest.

81
00:08:00.976 --> 00:08:06.657
"Let's pull ourselves together now. Look! It is quiet again.

82
00:08:06.658 --> 00:08:11.255
I think we should go back to check it out."

83
00:08:11.256 --> 00:08:15.228
"Then you go to the house first."

84
00:08:15.229 --> 00:08:20.763
"Okay, I'm not scared!"

85
00:08:20.764 --> 00:08:26.692
The robber entered the house quietly. He went into the kitchen to light a candle.

86
00:08:26.693 --> 00:08:34.501
But the cat was watching him. "Ah, there are two coals in the fireplace.

87
00:08:34.502 --> 00:08:39.131
I will strike my match on one of them."

88
00:08:39.132 --> 00:08:42.144
But the coals were really the cat's eyes.

89
00:08:42.145 --> 00:08:45.637
The robber struck the match on the cat's face.

90
00:08:45.638 --> 00:08:49.440
The cat hissed and scratched the robber's face.

91
00:08:49.441 --> 00:08:56.517
The frightened robber ran to the back door. There the dog bit his leg.

92
00:08:56.518 --> 00:09:00.680
The robber screamed and ran across the yard.

93
00:09:00.681 --> 00:09:03.694
The donkey woke up and kicked the robber.

94
00:09:03.695 --> 00:09:09.840
Then the rooster woke up. "Cock-a-doodle-doo!"

95
00:09:09.841 --> 00:09:13.963
The frightened robber ran to warn his friend.

96
00:09:13.964 --> 00:09:19.552
"Ah, there is a horrible witch sitting in the house.

97
00:09:19.553 --> 00:09:24.994
She hissed and scratched my face with her long claws.

98
00:09:24.995 --> 00:09:32.044
And by the door, a man with a knife stabbed me in the leg.

99
00:09:32.045 --> 00:09:36.836
When I ran outside, a black monster beat me with a club.

100
00:09:36.837 --> 00:09:45.226
A judge sat on the roof and called out, 'You are all robbers. Go away.'

101
00:09:45.227 --> 00:09:49.404
So I ran away as fast as I could."

102
00:09:49.405 --> 00:09:53.163
"We must escape before they come after us."

103
00:09:53.164 --> 00:10:01.027
So the robbers ran far away. The animals watched as the robbers ran away.

104
00:10:01.028 --> 00:10:03.493
"Hooray! The robbers are gone!"

105
00:10:03.494 --> 00:10:07.076
"This is a nice place to live. There is plenty to eat.

106
00:10:07.077 --> 00:10:11.920
And each of us has a warm place to sleep."

107
00:10:11.921 --> 00:10:14.643
"Let's stay here forever!"

108
00:10:14.644 --> 00:10:21.372
"Yes! Let's stay here. We can sing and eat all we want!

109
00:10:21.373 --> 00:10:27.122
We do not need to go to Bremen any longer."

110
00:10:27.123 --> 00:10:30.162
The robbers never returned to the house.

111
00:10:30.163 --> 00:10:46.743
And the four "musicians" lived in the house happily ever after.

